{title: Jingle Bells}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 1"}

[D]Dashing through the snow, in a one horse open [G]sleigh
[G]O'er the fields we [A]go, laughing all the [D]way
[D]Bells on bobtails ring, making spirits [G]bright
[G]What fun it is to [A]ride and sing, a [G]sleighing [A]song to[D]night

[A7]Ohhh

{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}

[D]Jingle bells, jingle bells, jingle [A7]all the [D]way
[G]Oh what fun it [D]is to ride in a [A]one-horse open [A7]sleigh
[D]Jingle bells, jingle bells, jingle [A7]all the [D]way
[G]Oh what fun it [D]is to ride in a [A]one-horse [A7]open [D]sleigh

{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 2"}

[D]A day or two ago, I thought I'd take a [G]ride
[G]And soon Miss Fanny [A]Bright, was seated by my [D]side
[D]The horse was lank and lean, misfortune seemed his [G]lot
[G]He got into a drifted [A]bank, and [G]then we [A]got up[D]sot

[A7]Ohhh

{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 3"}

[D]Now the ground is white, go it while you're [G]young
[G]Take the girls to[A]night, sing this sleighing [D]song
[D]Get a bobtailed bay, two-forty for his [G]speed
[G]Then hitch him to an open [A]sleigh, and [G]"Crack!" you'll [A]take the [D]lead

[A7]Ohhh

{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
